# text = I remember , the day they finished the malt-house , I thought summat great was to come of it ; for we'd a plum-pudding that day and a bit of a feast , and I said to my mother ,-- she was a fine dark-eyed woman , my mother was ,-- the little wench ' ull be as like her as two peas I was a little chap no higher much than my mother's knee ,-- she was sore fond of us children , Gritty and me ,-- and so I said to her , ' Mother ,' I said , ' shall we have plum-pudding _every_ day because o ' the malt-house ?
